    "body": "## Purpose\nStage the newly approved ZB architecture work **without touching the active CODE-ONLY bootstrap fix PR** and without changing current Control Tower runtime/state semantics.\n\n## Current sequencing rule\n\n1. Finish PR #8 (`fix/bootstrap-artifact-checks`) and get green checks.\n2. Merge only after its own required review/QC.\n3. Re-read the new protected `main` exact SHA.\n4. Create a fresh **docs/architecture-only branch from that exact protected main**.\n5. Add the staged architecture docs there.\n6. Run repository validation and independent review.\n7. Only then open isolated implementation proofs, one gate at a time.\n\nDo **not** mix these ideas into PR #8.\n\n## Authority boundaries that remain unchanged\n\n```text\nCHARACTER_DNA = anthropometric authority\nCHARACTER-SPECIFIC REST_RIG = skeletal authority\nBASE HUMAN / MORPH WEIGHTS / COMPILED BODY = derived\nUNRESOLVED stays unresolved\ncoordinate policy stays OPEN\nno OWNER LOCK\n```\n\n## Staged architecture directions\n\n### A. Babylon Parametric Human / Body Compiler\n\n```text\nREFERENCE EVIDENCE\n→ CHARACTER_DNA\n→ REST_RIG\n→ ANTHROPOMETRY SOLVER\n→ AUTHORING SHAPE BASIS\n→ COMPILED BODY MESH\n→ RUNTIME SKIN + SMALL CORRECTIVE SET\n→ CHARACTER SHELL\n→ ZB PRESENTATION\n```\n\n### B. OxiHuman donor/reference path\nUse only as a narrow replaceable backend candidate:\n\n```text\npinned CC0 body pack\n+ sparse morph engine\n+ measurement → fit → remeasure loop\n+ WASM geometry bridge\n+ provenance/hash discipline\n```\n\nReject as authority:\n- donor body parameters as Character Truth;\n- donor skeleton as skeletal truth;\n- current nearest-joint inverse-distance skin weights as production skinning;\n- whole repo as mandatory foundation before independent subset QC.\n\n### C. Motion Truth / Action Truth\n\n```text\nBODY TRUTH\n+ SPACE TRUTH\n+ MOTION TRUTH\n= ACTION TRUTH\n```\n\nLaws:\n- POSE IS NOT MOTION.\n- MOTION is transfer of mass, support and momentum through time.\n- ACTION is not an animation clip.\n- ANIMATION is one realization of ACTION TRUTH.\n\nCandidate phases:\n`PREPARE → LOAD → LAUNCH → AIR/TRANSFER → CONTACT → RECOVERY`\n\n### D. Cinematography Stack\n\n```text\nACTION TRUTH\n→ SHOT INTENT\n→ CAMERA TRUTH\n→ OPERATOR PERFORMANCE\n→ FRAME COMPOSITION\n→ VIEW PRESENTATION\n→ FRAME\n```\n\nLaws:\n- CAMERA DOES NOT FOLLOW ACTION. CAMERA INTERPRETS ACTION.\n- THE OPERATOR IS A PERFORMER.\n- CAMERA MOVEMENT MUST HAVE A REASON, A TARGET AND A SETTLE.\n- BIG HIT does not imply automatic camera shake.\n\n### E. ZB Core WASM direction\nPotential future math/compiler layer for anthropometry, measurements, morph/mesh compilation, surface anchors, kinematics and geometry QC. Babylon remains scene/render/animation/camera/presentation runtime.\n\n## Dependency policy\nPrefer: `CC0`, `MIT`, `BSD-2`, `BSD-3`, `Apache-2.0`, reviewed `MPL-2.0`.\nTreat `GPL`, `AGPL`, research-only and non-commercial model licenses as high-review / non-default.\n\nEvery production third-party body/morph/rig/solver asset must pin exact repo/revision/license/files/hashes and local derived hashes.\n\n## Implementation order\n\n```text\n0. finish current Control Tower bootstrap fix + QC\n1. docs-only integration PR from new protected main\n2. architecture boundary review\n3. OxiHuman/body donor proof O0\n4. Babylon Parametric Human proof B0\n5. Motion Truth proof M0\n6. Cinematography proof C1\n7. presentation/Grani only downstream of canonical truth\n```\n\n## Forbidden shortcuts\n- no architecture code in PR #8;\n- no Control Tower validator/state changes in staging docs PR;\n- no donor slider → DNA writeback;\n- no donor skeleton authority;\n- no UNRESOLVED promotion;\n- no early coordinate lock;\n- no experimental body/motion/camera code directly on `main`;\n- no OWNER LOCK from this issue or future docs review.\n\n## Expected next action after PR #8\nDJANGO should fetch the exact new protected `main` SHA and create a new docs-only branch from it. The branch should contain architecture documents only and must pass the existing repository validator before a separate review.",
